<title>Idle Rift RPG Privacy Policy</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bitter:wght@600;700&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@400;600&display=swap">

<style>
  /*
   * A public document a stranger opens on a phone, often in daylight — so it is
   * light by default and legible before it is characterful. The game's amber
   * shows up only as the accent, which is enough to tie it to the app without
   * making a legal notice look like a splash screen.
   */
  :root {
    --ground: #fbf9f5;
    --surface: #f3efe7;
    --line: #ddd5c7;
    --ink: #241f1a;
    --muted: #6b6055;
    --accent: #9a6b12;
    color-scheme: light dark;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme='light']) {
      --ground: #12100e;
      --surface: #1c1916;
      --line: #332d26;
      --ink: #e8dcc8;
      --muted: #9a8a76;
      --accent: #d9a441;
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme='dark'] {
    --ground: #12100e;
    --surface: #1c1916;
    --line: #332d26;
    --ink: #e8dcc8;
    --muted: #9a8a76;
    --accent: #d9a441;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--ground);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'Source Sans 3', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .wrap {
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 6rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  h1, h2 {
    font-family: Bitter, Georgia, serif;
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin: 0;
  }
  h1 { font-size: 2.4rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  p, ul { margin: 0; }
  section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.8rem; }
  ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
  li::marker { color: var(--accent); }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  strong { font-weight: 600; }

  .meta {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }
  hr.rule { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); margin: 0; }

  /* The one claim the whole document rests on, given its own weight. */
  .headline {
    background: var(--surface);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }

  footer {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .wrap { padding: 2.5rem 1.1rem 4rem; }
    h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; }
  }
</style>

<div class="wrap">

  <header>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Idle Rift RPG &middot; KOTM Studios &middot; Last updated 29 August 2026</p>
  </header>

  <p class="headline">
    <strong>Idle Rift RPG does not collect, store, or transmit any personal
    information.</strong> The game has no accounts, no sign-in, no advertising,
    and no analytics. Nothing you do in the game is sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <hr class="rule">

  <section>
    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>None.</p>
    <p>
      We do not ask for your name, email address, phone number, location, contacts,
      photos, or any other personal information. We do not assign you an advertising
      identifier, and we do not read the one your device already has.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the game stores on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Your progress is saved locally on your device so the game can continue where
      you left off. That save contains only game state:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your character's class, experience, level, and weapon skills</li>
      <li>Items, materials, gold, and potions you are carrying</li>
      <li>Which zones you have unlocked and which creatures you have studied</li>
      <li>Your game settings, such as potion thresholds</li>
      <li>A randomly generated character identifier, created on your device</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      That identifier is a random value with no connection to you, your device, or
      any account. It exists so the game can tell one character from another, and
      it never leaves your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      This data is held in your device's private app storage. No other app can read
      it, and we cannot read it either.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Network access</h2>
    <p>
      The app declares the Android <strong>Internet</strong> permission because the
      framework it is built on requires it in order to load the game's own files
      from inside the app package. The game makes no connections to any server, and
      transmits no data off your device. It is fully playable with your device
      offline or in airplane mode.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>
      The game contains no advertising networks, no analytics or measurement
      services, no crash reporting, and no social media integrations. No third
      party receives any information about you through this app.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you installed the game through Google Play, Google may collect information
      about the installation itself under
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's own privacy policy</a>.
      That is a function of the store, not of this game, and we receive none of it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The game does not knowingly collect information from anyone, of any age,
      because it does not collect information at all. There is nothing in it that
      would allow a child to disclose personal information: no chat, no user
      profiles, no user-generated content, and no way to contact other players.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>
      Because everything is stored on your device, you are always in control of it:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the in-game wipe option to erase your character and start fresh</li>
      <li>Clear the app's storage from your device's Settings</li>
      <li>Uninstall the app, which removes the save entirely</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      There is no server-side copy of anything, so there is nothing for us to delete
      on your behalf and no request you need to make.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If a future version of the game adds a feature that involves handling your
      data — cloud saves or leaderboards, for example — this policy will be updated
      before that version is released, and the change will be described in the
      release notes. The date at the top of this page always reflects the current
      version.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy can be sent to
      <a href="mailto:kotmstudios@gmail.com">kotmstudios@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr class="rule">

  <footer>
    Idle Rift RPG is developed by KOTM Studios.<br>
    Package name: com.kotmstudios.idleriftrpg
  </footer>

</div>
